Best For You Organics Company deploys a Microsoft Foundry resource (symbolic name account) and a project (symbolic name project) with system-assigned identities in main.bicep. The project managed identity must get the Foundry User role on the Foundry resource. The role definition ID of Foundry User is 53ca6127-db72-4b80-b1b0-d745d6d5456d.

How should you complete the Bicep code? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.

```bicep
resource foundryUser 'Microsoft.Authorization/roleDefinitions@2022-04-01' existing = {
  scope: [[1]]
  name: '53ca6127-db72-4b80-b1b0-d745d6d5456d'
}

resource projectFoundryUser 'Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments@2022-04-01' = {
  scope: account
  name: guid(account.id, project.id, foundryUser.id)
  properties: {
    roleDefinitionId: [[2]]
    principalId: [[3]]
    principalType: 'ServicePrincipal'
  }
}
```
